{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's motion and perception interface, separating motion commands from sensor outcomes. The specification encodes a conservative, coverage-oriented supervisor: random_walk is used for exploration in clear states, move_forward is used for short progress, and explicit turn recovery is used for obstacle events. Obstacle recovery states are one-shot and only allow the appropriate turn or scan. The supervisor always returns to exploration as soon as the path is clear, and never enables forward or random_walk in obstacle states.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for motion and perception to allow modular specification synthesis.",
    "Specification supervisor enforces: (1) random_walk in clear/search, (2) move_forward in short commit, (3) explicit turn recovery for obstacles, (4) immediate return to exploration after path_clear, (5) no forward/random_walk in obstacle states, (6) no oscillatory or idle loops."
  ],
